spec:
  grid: odd square, 7-15 rows/cols
  background: 0 (black)
  border: 1-cell bg border on all four sides
  masks:
    count: 3-5 distinct non-bg colors
    layout: vertically stacked with no gaps; bboxes tile rows 1..H-2 exactly
    centering: every bbox horizontally centered on grid center [observed]
    bbox_height: 1-4 rows each
    bbox_width: odd, 3-11; always <= grid_width - 2
    horizontal_symmetry: all masks are LR-symmetric [observed]
    vertical_symmetry: majority (>=50%) of masks are NOT vertically symmetric
    pixel_density: 0.39-1.00 within bbox
    connectivity: 1-5 connected components per mask (4-conn)
  transform: each mask is reflected top-to-bottom within its own bbox (row r -> r0+r1-r)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (no inversion needed; transform is simple per-mask vertical flip)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N (odd, 7-15). Pick K colors (3-5 distinct, non-zero).
    2. Partition inner height (N-2) into K bbox heights (each 1-4, sum = N-2).
    3. For each mask, pick an odd bbox width (3-11, <= N-2), centered in the grid.
    4. Generate an LR-symmetric binary mask within the bbox with density 0.39-1.0.
       Ensure at least ceil(K/2) masks are NOT vertically symmetric.
    5. Place masks on a bg grid at consecutive row bands starting at row 1.
    6. Validate no pixel collisions (guaranteed by construction since bboxes are disjoint).
```
